==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Flamenco Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bellydance Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Matador Cat has the niche of [[:Category:Cats with Dodge Attack ability|dodging]] the attacks of [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, a rare one in the Cat Army. However, its usage is limited by the low activation chance (30%), low health and high cost of 540¢. The cooldown doesn't help either. Because of this, Matador is outclassed by many other cats at its role, such as [[Viking Cat (Rare Cat)|Thor Cat]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]] and often generalist meatshields too. Because of this, its use is only recommended in complete absence of alternatives.

==='''True Form'''===
Improved speed and health bring little to Bellydance Cat, who stays too weak relative to her cost for her stats to really matter. As such, it is not recommended to give much priority to this evolution, unless one plans to invest in her Talents.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]''' makes her a viable meatshield in several Aku-centered stages, as Aku enemies typically have [[Shield]]s, meaning most other crowd-controlling options tend not to work if not aided by [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]]. The scenarios where this will see use remains rare, but can occasionally prove helpful if it triggers, mainly in pure Red/Aku stages, or those that mix them, such as [[Wrath of Hell (Deadly)|Wrath of Hell]] and [[Okame's Teahouse (Merciless)|Okame's Teahouse]]. '''Slow''' is hard to utilize because of her short range, meaning that most enemies would be standing still anyway if Bellydance could hit them, plus there are far better options for anti-Red crowd control. '''Resist Freeze''' is meant to improve her performance in presence of [[Cerberus Kids]], [[Wicked Face]], [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] or [[Dark Emperor Santa]] and in some specific situations, but it's unlikely to make much of a difference; it should, therefore, be unlocked only if a situation calls for it. '''HP Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' are good boosts for this unit, but not worth it unless she is already boosted by + levels.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

